{"assets":["/statement-assets/288c18f73025ed5699f6c352ede3ec260e240b63815f16e3291b1f06d56dece6.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"177","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B1. Rectangular Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Smart Beaver from ABBYY decided to have a day off. But doing nothing the whole day turned out to be too boring, and he decided to play a game with pebbles. Initially, the Beaver has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" pebbles. He arranges them in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" equal rows, each row has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" pebbles ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a > 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Note that the Beaver must use all the pebbles he has, i. e. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n = a·b"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/288c18f73025ed5699f6c352ede3ec260e240b63815f16e3291b1f06d56dece6.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" 10 pebbles are arranged in two rows, each row has 5 pebbles "}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Once the Smart Beaver has arranged the pebbles, he takes back any of the resulting rows (that is, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" pebbles) and discards all other pebbles. Then he arranges "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" his pebbles again (possibly choosing other values of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":") and takes back one row, and so on. The game continues until at some point the Beaver ends up with exactly one pebble. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The game process can be represented as a finite sequence of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1, ..., ck"},{"kind":"text","text":", where: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1 = n"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the number of pebbles that the Beaver ends up with after the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th move, that is, the number of pebbles in a row after some arrangement of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" pebbles ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ i < k"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Note that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci > ci + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ck = 1"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The result of the game is the sum of numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":". You are given "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Find the maximum possible result of the game."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The single line of the input contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the initial number of pebbles the Smart Beaver has."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input limitations for getting 30 points are: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 50"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input limitations for getting 100 points are: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 109"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — the maximum possible result of the game."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"16\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"15\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first example ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1 = 10"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The possible options for the game development are:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Arrange the pebbles in 10 rows, one pebble per row. Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c2 = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the game ends after the first move with the result of 11. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Arrange the pebbles in 5 rows, two pebbles per row. Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c2 = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the game continues. During the second move we have two pebbles which can be arranged in a unique way (remember that you are not allowed to put all the pebbles in the same row!) — 2 rows, one pebble per row. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c3 = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the game ends with the result of 13. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Finally, arrange the pebbles in two rows, five pebbles per row. The same logic leads us to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c2 = 5, c3 = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the game ends with the result of 16 — the maximum possible result. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B1","problemCode":"177B1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/177/problem/B1"}